          "_key": "s7jm",
          "text": "Wrongful death expenses",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7jp",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7jo",
          "text": "Punitive damages",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7jr",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7jq",
          "text": "Do not accept a settlement offered to you by an insurance company for your personal injury claim until you’ve spoken to an attorney at Dormer Harpring, LLC. There is no financial risk in contacting us, as we offer free initial consultations. We will go over the settlement offer and evaluate your case to determine if you are being offered a fair financial recovery. If not, we can take over insurance negotiations on your behalf to fight for greater compensation.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7jt",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7js",
          "text": "Do I Have a Case?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7jv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7ju",
          "text": "You might have grounds to file a personal injury claim in Colorado if one or more parties caused or contributed to your accident. If a party using an ordinary amount of care would have been able to prevent your injury, the defendant in question is most likely financially responsible (liable) for your injuries and related losses, including medical expenses and property repairs.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7k0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l7jx",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/but-for_test"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7jw",
          "text": "Many plaintiffs use the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7jy",
          "text": "“but for” test",
          "marks": [
            "l7jx"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7jz",
          "text": " to determine if they can hold someone liable for an accident. Is it true that you would not be currently injured but for the defendant’s action or omission? If the answer is yes, you may be eligible for financial compensation through a civil claim. To find out if your case has merit, arrange a consultation with our Thornton personal injury lawyers.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7k2",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7k1",
          "text": "Colorado Statute of Limitations",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7k7",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l7k4",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://leg.colorado.gov/publications/statutes-limitations"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7k3",
          "text": "In Colorado, injury victims need to be aware of the time limit to file a personal injury lawsuit. According to the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7k5",
          "text": "Colorado personal injury statute of limitations",
          "marks": [
            "l7k4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7k6",
          "text": ", injury victims have two years from the date the injury occurred to file a lawsuit in civil court. If a victim fails to file a lawsuit within the time frame, it may be more difficult for them to recover any compensation for their losses.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7k9",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7k8",
          "text": "Contact Our Thornton, CO Personal Injury Attorneys Today",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7ke",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l7kb",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/contact/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7ka",
          "text": "You are not alone as the injured victim of a personal injury accident in Colorado. The Thornton personal injury attorneys at Dormer Harpring, LLC can work closely with you to pursue justice. We care about our clients in Adams County and the journeys that they are on. We will do what is necessary to help you achieve your case goals. Discuss how we can help you in more detail by calling (303) 747-4404 or ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7kc",
          "text": "contacting us online",
          "marks": [
            "l7kb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7kd",
          "text": " today to arrange a free consultation and get the legal representation you deserve.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
